DESCRIPTION:Event information: https://www.un.org/digital-emerging-technologies/content/open-source-week-2025\n\nUN Open Source Week 2025 facilitates global dialogue and collaboration on open source\, digital public infrastructure (DPI)\, and the development of innovative solutions to global challenges. Since its inception in 2023\, the event has captured significant international attention\, reflecting strong demand for a UN-led forum on open source and digital cooperation.\n\nThis year’s conference expands to a multi-day format from 16–20 June 2025 that will include our UN Tech Over on 16 – 17 June\, the return of OSPOs for Good on 18 June\, Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI Day) on 19 June\, and Side Events on 20 June. This evolved program will offer increased opportunities for ideation\, co-creation\, and meaningful networking in response to the ecosystem's growing demand for deeper engagement.\n\nUN Open Source Week will feature a full week of networking\, insightful panels\, a hackathon\, and breakout sessions exploring topics related to open source\, digital public infrastructure\, problem solving\, and digital cooperation. This is an opportunity to learn from and connect with fellow industry professionals while deepening understanding of open source and its global potential.
DTEND:20250620T000000Z
LOCATION:New York & Online
DTSTART:20250616T000000Z
SUMMARY:UN Open Source Week
UID:3d33c360-9bbc-4251-abd6-e3860d38c2cb@3d33.org
END:VEVENT
