CATEGORIES:open software
DESCRIPTION:Event Website: https://events.linuxfoundation.org/open-source-summit-north-america/\n\nOpen Source Summit (formerly LinuxCon) is a name for a series of annual conventions organized each year since 2009 by the Linux Foundation. The first LinuxCon took place in North America. Linux Foundation started organizing similar events in Europe and Japan.\n\nApart from keynotes given by some high-profile Linux people (such as Linus Torvalds or Greg Kroah-Hartman in 2009)\, Open Source Summit is increasingly used as a platform for open source thought leaders\, influencers\, hiring managers\, professionals\, and developers in Information technology to talk about their plans for the technological landscape and announce major news.\n\nSrc: Wikipédia
DTEND:20250625T000000Z
LOCATION:Denver
DTSTART:20250623T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Source Summit America
UID:3e80b0cb-47b6-4dae-9969-514c6596baa5@3e80.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:open software
DESCRIPTION:Event Website: https://events.linuxfoundation.org/open-source-summit-europe/\n\nOpen Source Summit (formerly LinuxCon) is a name for a series of annual conventions organized each year since 2009 by the Linux Foundation. The first LinuxCon took place in North America. Linux Foundation started organizing similar events in Europe and Japan.\n\nApart from keynotes given by some high-profile Linux people (such as Linus Torvalds or Greg Kroah-Hartman in 2009)\, Open Source Summit is increasingly used as a platform for open source thought leaders\, influencers\, hiring managers\, professionals\, and developers in Information technology to talk about their plans for the technological landscape and announce major news.\n\nSrc: Wikipédia
DTEND:20250827T000000Z
LOCATION:Amsterdam
DTSTART:20250825T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Source Summit Europe
UID:2c39272c-36ce-44e0-ad62-798d5d471cc0@2c39.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:open education,open science,open software
DESCRIPTION:Site évènement : https://libreabc.ch\n\nLibreABC est un événement qui se déroule sur une journée et qui propose des ateliers\, conférences et débats autour des logiciels et de la culture du libre dans le monde des archives\, des bibliothèques et des centres de documentation.\n\nUn évènement en collaboration entre le canton de Genève\, hautes-école et université.
DTEND:20250909T000000Z
LOCATION:Geneva
DTSTART:20250909T000000Z
SUMMARY:Journée des logiciels libres en Archives\, Bibliothèques et Centres de documentation
UID:e3f514d2-b82f-4832-8ec3-7e84ad330449@e3f5.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:open science
DESCRIPTION:Event website: https://www.open-science-conference.eu/\n\nThe Open Science Conference is an annual international conference dedicated to the Open Science movement. It provides a unique forum for researchers\, data stewards\, librarians\, practitioners\, infrastructure providers\, policy makers\, and other important stakeholders to discuss the latest and future developments in Open Science. In 2025\, the conference returns to its roots and takes place as a face-to-face event in Hamburg again.\n\nThis year’s conference will have a special focus on the intersection between Open Science and AI. The rapid integration of artificial intelligence and corresponding tools into scientific research poses both new challenges but also opportunities for Open Science practices. This requires a reflection on how this can be aligned with transparency\, accessibility\, reproducibility\, and reusability as core principles of Open Science.
DTEND:20251009T000000Z
LOCATION:Hamburg\, Germany
DTSTART:20251008T000000Z
SUMMARY:The international Open Science Conference
UID:45181765-7888-46b0-a070-ae484f19084b@4518.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:open models
DESCRIPTION:Event information: https://2025.allthingsopen.org/\n\nAfter all these years\, open source skills are more important and sought after than ever.\n\nMore than anything\, ATO is an educational conference where attendees learn about new technologies and topics\, and it’s always been that way. The goal is for attendees to leave having learned something or been made aware of something new.
DTEND:20251014T000000Z
LOCATION:Raleigh\, USA
DTSTART:20251012T000000Z
SUMMARY:All Things Open
UID:4a107b89-ff63-4f31-992f-7d9d6e53a98d@4a10.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:open science
DESCRIPTION:Open Access Week is an opportunity for the academic and research community to continue to learn about the potential benefits of Open Access\, to share what they’ve learned with colleagues\, and to help inspire wider participation in helping to make Open Access a new norm in scholarship and research.\n\nOpen Access to information – the free\, immediate\, online access to the results of scholarly research\, and the right to use and re-use those results as you need – has the power to transform the way research and scientific inquiry are conducted. It has direct and widespread implications for academia\, medicine\, science\, industry\, and for society as a whole.\n\nOpen Access Week is an invaluable chance to connect the global momentum toward the open sharing of knowledge with the advancement of policy changes and the importance of social issues affecting people around the world. The event is celebrated by individuals\, institutions and organizations around the world.
DTEND:20251026T000000Z
LOCATION:https://www.openaccessweek.org/
DTSTART:20251020T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Access Week
UID:9ea312b5-776c-4015-b40c-642c05865116@9ea3.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:open education
DESCRIPTION:Event information : https://openeducationconference.org/\n\nThe Open Education Conference (“OpenEd”) is an annual convening for sharing and learning about open educational resources\, open pedagogy\, and open education initiatives. This engaging event brings together over 1\,600 educators and open education advocates in-person and online to collaborate\, support\, and drive strategies for education that are accessible\, affordable\, and reflective of the learners they serve.\n\nThe Open Education Conference community has gathered annually since 2004—originally in person\, then online\, and now as an inclusive hybrid event. Deeply rooted in the community\, the conference is led by a community-elected   and driven by a shared  . Conference operations are currently housed within SPARC.
DTEND:20251030T000000Z
LOCATION:Denver & Online
DTSTART:20251028T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Education Conference
UID:b4771d76-ddd0-4db8-9440-a0a39b883f19@b477.org
END:VEVENT
